  "description": "Determine if a string follows a given pattern using backtracking.",
  "target": "pattern: 'abab', s: 'redblueredblue'",
  "pseudocode": "1. map = {}, set = {}\n2. function backtrack(pIdx, sIdx):\n3. if pIdx == len(pattern) and sIdx == len(s): return True\n4. char = pattern[pIdx]\n5. for end = sIdx + 1 to len(s):\n6. sub = s[sIdx:end]\n7. if char in map and map[char] == sub: backtrack(pIdx + 1, end)\n8. else if char not in map and sub not in set: add to map/set, backtrack(pIdx + 1, end), remove from map/set",
